Homepage: https://github.com/FreeMixer/plugin-hostd
Description: supervisor of LV2 and CLAP plugin hosts behind one mod-host socket
 plugin-hostd speaks mod-host's socket protocol to a controller and runs one
 worker process per plugin, or per named pool of plugins, behind it: mod-host
 for LV2 plugins and omx-clap-host for CLAP plugins. A plugin that crashes
 takes down its own worker and nothing else, and the daemon puts it back.
 Audio never passes through the daemon: every worker is a JACK client, as in
 mod-host.
 .
 A format whose worker is not installed refuses its adds; the other format
 is unaffected. mod-host is not packaged by Debian: install it from source
 for LV2 plugins.

